WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/VehicleHeader.tsx — a presentational vehicle-detail header
  (named export) rendered by the vehicle-detail page. Props: { vehicle?, state?, onRefetchState }.
  Imports Button (@/components/ui), FadeIn (@/components/motion), StatusBadge (@/components/data-display),
  useWakeVehicle + getVehicleStatus (@/api/hooks/useVehicles), useTranslation. It renders ONE horizontal row
  (flex items-center gap-4):
    1. back  : <Link to="/vehicles"> wrapping an ArrowLeft glyph.
    2. title : <h1 text-3xl font-bold> = vehicle?.display_name || vehicle?.vin || t('common.vehicle','Vehicle').
    3. badge : <StatusBadge status={vehicle ? getVehicleStatus(state) : 'offline'} size="md" /> — the dot color +
               capitalized label come from the FSM state registry (types/fsm/vehicle.ts VEHICLE_STATE_ENTRIES).
    4. sub   : <p text-sm> = {vehicle?.model} {vehicle?.trim_badging} &middot; <span font-mono>{vehicle?.vin}</span>.
    5. wake  : <Button icon={<Power/>} loading={wakeMut.isPending}>{t('common.wakeUp','Wake Up')}</Button>;
               handleWake → wakeMut.mutate(vehicleId, { onSuccess: setTimeout(onRefetchState, 5000) }).
  Data sources (prompt): useVehicles, useTranslation, useWakeVehicle. Status derivation (api/types.ts L980
  deriveVehicleStatus): !state→offline · is_charging→charging · speed>0→driving · state∈VEHICLE_STATES→that ·
  else→online; the header guards `vehicle ? … : 'offline'`. i18n keys extracted from source: common.vehicle
  ("Vehicle") + common.wakeUp ("Wake Up"). Reproduced 1:1 (covenant pt 2). The web child has no loading/empty/
  error branch of its own (it renders with optional chaining); the P4 leaf states (loading/empty/error) +
  the stale/offline connectivity axis are the sanctioned leaf additions, every one rendering (no hidden surface).

